---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/FunnelLayout.astro';
import OneClickOffer from '../../../components/funnel/OneClickOffer.astro';
import { PHOTOS } from '../../../components/clients/firstshares/photos';
---
<Layout client="firstshares" funnel="checkout" step="upsell" title="One thing before you go" noindex bare>
  <OneClickOffer client="firstshares" funnel="checkout" kind="upsell" priceKey="upsell" eyebrow="Your order is confirmed. One thing before you go." headline="Get your questions answered live, every two weeks, for three months." price="$197" compareAt="$390" bullets={['6 live group calls with Maya, every two weeks.', 'Bring your screen, share it, and get it walked through (education, not personal advice).', 'Every call recorded and indexed.', 'A members-only thread between calls, with a 48-hour answer.', 'A 3-month nudge: is your transfer still running?']} acceptLabel="Yes, add First Shares Live · $197" declineLabel="No thanks, I’ll work through it on my own" acceptNext="/firstshares/checkout/thanks" declineNext="/firstshares/checkout/downsell">
    <Fragment slot="top"><img src={PHOTOS.mayaBoard} alt="Maya Okafor at a maths blackboard" width="2000" height="1333" class="h-48 w-full rounded-xl object-cover object-[40%_30%] sm:h-64" /></Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="why"><p>You’re about to open accounts you’ve never opened, in a menu you’ve never seen. Most students get stuck on one specific screen: a 401(k) fund list with 31 options, a rollover form, a “settlement fund.” In First Shares Live you bring that screen to a group call with Maya every two weeks for three months, and leave with it done.</p></Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="objection"><p><strong>If you’re not sure you’ll need it,</strong> that’s normal. It’s insurance against the one screen that stops you. If you never get stuck, the calls are where you hear the questions other people asked, and that’s usually the one you didn’t know to ask. $197 today instead of $390.</p></Fragment>
  </OneClickOffer>
</Layout>
